KG42.register("rules-81470d251d748f8beb9ef162",{"id":"05-double_auction::v141-c-R016","paper":"05-double_auction","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R016","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M03","name":"Energy-trade execution","process_stage":"activation","market_meaning":"Execution of the VCG transaction requires the market operator's monetary contribution to cover the trading deficit. Scope: VCG transactions with a deficit between buyer payments and seller receipts. Condition: The price paid by trading buyers is less than the price received by trading sellers.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function execution.energy_trade under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["execution.energy_trade","settlement.payment"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R016-E001","source":"execution.energy_trade","target":"settlement.payment","type":"requires","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R016-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-07"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"VCG transactions with a deficit between buyer payments and seller receipts.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-07"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R016-C001","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"Execution of the VCG transaction requires the market operator's monetary contribution to cover the trading deficit. Scope: VCG transactions with a deficit between buyer payments and seller receipts. Condition: The price paid by trading buyers is less than the price received by trading sellers.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-07"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-07","location":{"location_id":"src-22913ad574-p03-c1r1__v141-a-M03-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1","anchor_text":"J. Lin, et al. and S P are the bid and ask prices at the largest breakeven index, re- 2. spectively.","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The Vickrey-Clark-Groves (VCG) mechanism is an alternative auction mechanism that maximizes social welfare and motivates participants to bid truthfully at the expense of the market operator [46]. $B_{\\gamma+1}^P$ and $S_{\\gamma+1}^P$ are the bid and ask prices following the largest breakeven index, respectively. Effectively, $B_{\\gamma}^P \\geq B_{\\gamma+1}^P$ and $S_{\\gamma}^P \\leq S_{\\gamma+1}^P$ due to the natural ordering rule for sorting offers. Since the price that trading buyers pay is less than the price that trading sellers receive, there exists a deficit that needs to be subsidized by the market operator to facilitate the transaction."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"No design-selection or operational decision variable is defined in the frozen graph or source text for this rule. The quantities relevant to the deficit condition (buyer payment rate, seller receipt rate) are outcomes of the VCG payment rules, not variables chosen in this execution rule, and the frozen graph provides no x objects for this rule.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed parameter is defined in the frozen graph or source text for this rule. The source passage mentions transaction-dependent bid/ask prices and a deficit, not fixed inputs, and the frozen graph provides no theta objects for this rule."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M03-clearing","v141-a-M03-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"execution.energy_trade","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-07","quote":"Since the price that trading buyers pay is less than the price that trading sellers receive, there exists a deficit that needs to be subsidized by the market operator to facilitate the transaction."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"3168683367f203cf4247a87b7cf52aa13b4e8c1f0e75bf3547737c10280ece35","applicability":"needs_revision","reason":"The rule states a mathematical/economic condition for VCG execution: the market operator must subsidize the trading deficit when the price paid by trading buyers is less than the price received by trading sellers. The frozen graph for this rule contains only execution.energy_trade and settlement.payment nodes and a requires edge. It lacks typed symbols for the buyer payment rate, the seller receipt rate, and the deficit quantity needed to transcribe the source inequality and deficit condition. The existing constraint v141-c-R016-C001 therefore remains not_formalized rather than being replaced with invented mathematics.","bindings":[],"revision_requests":["C.1: extend the frozen graph for v141-c-R016 with typed symbols for the buyer payment rate p_buy and seller receipt rate p_sell (unit $/kWh), and a deficit quantity D = p_sell - p_buy, bound to settlement.payment and execution.energy_trade, with same-mechanism evidence v141-b-g01-ev-07 and, if approved, v141-b-g01-ev-05 for the VCG price expressions.","C.1: alternatively, approve a procedural formalization of the operator-contribution requirement that does not require price symbols, if the graphers judge the deficit condition to be outside this rule's mathematical scope.","B: the source text for v141-b-g01-ev-07 is unreviewed and contains an unresolved index ambiguity noted in v141-b-g01-ev-05 (Table 1 VCG buyer-payment term prints S^P without a subscript). Source verification is required before any strict inequality or numeric deficit formalization."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
